instruction:
Bug fix in the Go repo at /echo (labstack/echo v4). Do NOT modify any *_test.go file. Do NOT touch any file other than /echo/context.go.

BUG: `func (c *context) Scheme()` in /echo/context.go (around lines 252-271) returns the raw value of the `X-Forwarded-Proto` / `X-Forwarded-Protocol` / `X-Url-Scheme` headers without validating it. Expected behaviour (from hidden tests `TestContext_Scheme/ignores_invalid_X-Forwarded-Proto_and_uses_X-Forwarded_Protocol` and `TestContext_Scheme/ignores_invalid_forwarded_headers_and_falls_back_to_http`): an invalid scheme value in those headers must be IGNORED, so that the next header in the priority chain is consulted, and if none yields a valid scheme the function falls back to "http". Only "http" and "https" (case-insensitive) are valid values; a valid value must still be returned as-is (unchanged behaviour for valid input).

REQUIRED EDIT (only in /echo/context.go): keep the existing order (IsTLS -> X-Forwarded-Proto -> X-Forwarded-Protocol -> X-Forwarded-Ssl=="on" -> X-Url-Scheme -> "http") but only return a header value when it is a valid scheme. Add a small unexported helper in context.go, e.g.:

	// isValidScheme reports whether the given value is a valid HTTP scheme (http or https).
	func isValidScheme(scheme string) bool {
		return strings.EqualFold(scheme, "http") || strings.EqualFold(scheme, "https")
	}

and use it for the X-Forwarded-Proto, X-Forwarded-Protocol and X-Url-Scheme headers (leave the X-Forwarded-Ssl == "on" check as is). `strings` is already imported in context.go. Keep gofmt-clean.

VERIFICATION (report exact commands and output):
1. `cd /echo && gofmt -l context.go` (must print nothing), `go build ./... && go vet ./...`.
2. Baseline first: run `cd /echo && go test ./... -count=1` BEFORE your edit and record failures; then run it again after your edit and report the full summary. The pre-existing `TestContext_Scheme` (in context_test.go) must still pass — it covers: TLS->https, X-Forwarded-Proto "https"->https, X-Forwarded-Protocol "http"->http, X-Forwarded-Ssl "on"->https, X-Url-Scheme "https"->https, nothing->http.
3. Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/zz_tmp_scheme_test.go (package echo) with tests that reproduce the two hidden subtests: (a) request with Header X-Forwarded-Proto = "invalid" and X-Forwarded-Protocol = "https" must yield "https"; (b) request with X-Forwarded-Proto = "invalid", X-Forwarded-Protocol = "invalid", X-Forwarded-Ssl = "invalid", X-Url-Scheme = "invalid" must yield "http". Build the context as `&context{request: &http.Request{Header: http.Header{...}}}` like the existing TestContext_Scheme does. Run `cd /echo && go test -run 'TmpScheme' -v -count=1 .` and report. THEN DELETE the temp file and confirm with `git status --short` that the only modified files are context.go and middleware/proxy.go (proxy.go is modified by someone else — leave it alone; ignore untracked zz_*.go files created by other agents, do NOT delete them).

Report the exact `git diff context.go` and all command outputs.

URGENT bug fix in the Go repo at /echo (labstack/echo v4). Do NOT modify any *_test.go file. Do NOT touch any file other than /echo/bind.go.

BUG: In `func (b *DefaultBinder) bindData` in /echo/bind.go the map branch (around lines 127-133) is:

	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
		return nil
	}

This only supports maps whose element type is a single string; binding into a `map[string][]string` destination panics (`reflect.Set: value of type string is not assignable to type []string`). A hidden test `TestDefaultBinder_bindDataToMap` with subtest `ok, bind to map[string][]string` must pass, while binding into `map[string]string` must keep working (first value of the slice).

REQUIRED EDIT (only in /echo/bind.go): replace the map branch body with an element-kind aware version, e.g.:

	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			if typ.Elem().Kind() == reflect.Slice {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v))
			} else {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
			}
		}
		return nil
	}

Keep it gofmt-clean. Do not change any other behavior.

VERIFICATION (report exact commands and output):
1. `cd /echo && gofmt -l bind.go` (must print nothing) and `go build ./... && go vet ./...`.
2. `cd /echo && go test ./... -count=1` — report the full summary. IMPORTANT: before your edit, also run this once and record which tests fail (baseline), so you can prove you did not break anything.
3. Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/zz_tmp_bindmap_test.go (package echo) with a test that does: `b := new(DefaultBinder); m := map[string][]string{}; err := b.bindData(&m, map[string][]string{"a": {"1", "2"}, "b": {"3"}}, "query")` and asserts no error and `m["a"] == []string{"1","2"}` and `m["b"] == []string{"3"}`. Also add a second test binding into `map[string]string` asserting first-value semantics (`m["a"] == "1"`), and a third binding into `map[string]interface{}` asserting it does not panic. Run `cd /echo && go test -run 'TmpBindMap' -v -count=1 .` and report. THEN DELETE the temp file (`rm -f /echo/zz_tmp_bindmap_test.go`) and confirm with `git status --short` that the ONLY modified file is bind.go (note: middleware/proxy.go is also modified by someone else — leave it alone; there may also be untracked zz_*.go files created by another agent — do NOT delete those, they are not yours).
4. Also check whether any pre-existing test in the repo binds into a map: `cd /echo && grep -rn 'map\[string\]' bind_test.go binder_test.go | head -30` and report.

Report the exact `git diff bind.go`, all command outputs, and the baseline vs after test results.

Bug fix in the Go repo at /echo (labstack/echo v4). Do NOT modify any *_test.go file. Do NOT touch any file other than /echo/middleware/compress.go. Be quick and focused; you have limited time.

CONTEXT: A bug was deliberately injected into /echo/middleware/compress.go (the Gzip middleware). A hidden test `TestGzipEmpty` (package middleware) must pass after your fix; it is not in the repo. All pre-existing tests currently pass (`go test ./... -count=1` is green), so the injected bug lies in a code path NOT covered by the existing tests: the path where the handler writes ZERO bytes through the gzip writer.

HYPOTHESIS TO VERIFY EMPIRICALLY: when the handler writes an empty byte slice (e.g. `c.String(http.StatusOK, "")`, `c.Blob(http.StatusOK, echo.MIMETextPlainCharsetUTF8, []byte{})`, or `c.Response().Write([]byte{})`), the gzip.Writer lazily emits its 10-byte gzip header into the real ResponseWriter, so the response body is NOT empty (it starts with 0x1f 0x8b) even though `res.Size == 0` and the middleware's own comment says the response must be reset "to it's pristine state when nothing is written to body".

STEPS:
1. Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/middleware/zz_tmp_gzipempty_test.go (package middleware) that, for each of these handlers, runs `Gzip()` middleware with a request carrying `Accept-Encoding: gzip` and an httptest recorder, and prints/asserts `rec.Body.Len()`, the first bytes of the body, `rec.Header().Get(echo.HeaderContentEncoding)` and `rec.Header().Get(echo.HeaderContentType)`:
   (a) handler returns nil without writing anything;
   (b) handler calls `c.NoContent(http.StatusOK)`;
   (c) handler calls `c.String(http.StatusOK, "")`;
   (d) handler calls `c.Response().Write([]byte{})`;
   (e) handler calls `c.Response().Write([]byte("test"))` (control).
   Run `cd /echo && go test ./middleware/ -run TmpGzipEmpty -v -count=1` and report the exact output.
2. Confirm which cases produce a non-empty body (expect (c) and (d) to produce ~10 bytes starting with 0x1f 0x8b). That is the bug.
3. FIX (minimal, in /echo/middleware/compress.go only): make `func (w *gzipResponseWriter) Write(b []byte) (int, error)` a no-op for empty input, e.g. add at the top:

	if len(b) == 0 {
		return 0, nil
	}

   so that nothing is handed to the gzip writer, `res.Size` stays 0, and the middleware's deferred cleanup restores the pristine response (no Content-Encoding, empty body). Do not change behaviour for non-empty writes. Keep gofmt-clean (`gofmt -l middleware/compress.go` must print nothing).
4. VERIFY: re-run the temp test (cases (c) and (d) must now give an empty body and empty Content-Encoding; case (e) must still return valid gzip data decompressing to "test"), then run `cd /echo && go test ./middleware/ -run 'TestGzip' -v -count=1` and `cd /echo && go test ./... -count=1` and report the summaries. All pre-existing tests MUST still pass.
5. DELETE the temp file (`rm -f /echo/middleware/zz_tmp_gzipempty_test.go`) and confirm `git status --short` shows middleware/compress.go modified and no *_test.go modified (other agents may have modified bind.go, context.go, middleware/proxy.go and left untracked zz_*.go files — leave those alone).

Report: the exact `git diff middleware/compress.go`, the observed before/after bodies for each case, and all command outputs. If your empirical findings contradict the hypothesis, say so explicitly and report what you actually observed instead of guessing.
